* text=auto eol=lf
*.go text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

# Generated files — exclude from language stats and diff context.
# -text skips line-ending normalization: go mod vendor copies upstream
# content verbatim, and a few modules ship CRLF. Without -text every
# vendor refresh rewrites those files to LF and breaks the vendor-tidy
# drift check.
vendor/** linguist-vendored -text
go.sum -diff
*.lock -diff
# The mise lockfiles are the exception to the -diff rule above: they
# hold the toolchain download digests, and a version bump's diff is the
# only place a reviewer sees those digests change. The bare basename
# matches both ./mise.lock and .config/mise/mise.lock.
mise.lock diff
# Conflict resolution policy, read by the resolve-rebase-conflicts skill
# through `git check-attr rebase-resolve`. apm regenerates this lockfile
# wholesale, so merging two versions of it produces something neither
# side wrote. The skill takes one side, and `apm install` after the
# rebase writes the real answer.
apm.lock.yaml rebase-resolve=regenerate
# tools/skill-tokens.sh writes these, and two branches that both touched
# a skill body produce two different measurements of it. Neither is the
# answer; re-running the recipe is.
**/skills/*/tokens.json rebase-resolve=regenerate
# tools/generate-skills.sh writes these from packages/agents/source/skills.
# Merging two versions of generated output produces something the
# generator never wrote, so a conflict takes one side whole and
# `mise run generate-skills` writes the real answer afterwards. One line
# per migrated skill, because a skill not yet migrated is hand-maintained
# and its conflicts need judgement. The deployed copies follow from the
# packages through `apm install`.
